# M36 (D42) — same target/shape as bench-60.tflw but a single VU (no concurrency at all), to test
# whether tflw's own per-iteration dispatch/scheduling overhead balloons specifically under
# real concurrent VU load (60 VUs contending for the same single-threaded event loop) versus
# staying flat like M35a-2's own 1-VU/78.9%-idle isolation test found for per-call CPU cost.

test "concurrency ground truth solo"
  ramp to 1 users over 20s
  api GET /products
  expect status equals 200
  capture body[0].id as productId
  api POST /orders body { items: [{ productId: {productId}, quantity: 1 }] }
  expect status equals 201
